FORM S-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: statutes-of-schedules.
FILED BY: the legislature, one section at a time, like the wall.

INCORPORATE BY REFERENCE statutes-of-arithmetic.

OFF THE RECORD: The statutes of schedules. This statute stands on the
OFF THE RECORD: statutes of arithmetic (greatest-of petitions maximum),
OFF THE RECORD: and any case that incorporates this statute receives
OFF THE RECORD: the arithmetic transitively, spliced once, however
OFF THE RECORD: many roads lead to it.
OFF THE RECORD:
OFF THE RECORD: A caution on equality: tally-of and containment-of
OFF THE RECORD: compare with EQUAL, and comparing values of different
OFF THE RECORD: standing is a verdict. Search a heterogeneous schedule
OFF THE RECORD: only for what you are prepared to be compared with.

THE OFFICE OF total-of, CONCERNING entries.
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF total-from REGARDING entries AND 1.

THE OFFICE OF total-from, CONCERNING entries AND index.
    SHOULD index EXCEED THE LENGTH OF entries, REMAND WITH 0.
    REMAND WITH (THE ITEM AT index IN entries) PLUS (THE FINDING OF total-from REGARDING entries AND index PLUS 1).

THE OFFICE OF greatest-of, CONCERNING entries.
    SHOULD THE LENGTH OF entries EQUAL 0, HOLD "the greatest item of an empty schedule; the Court declines to rank nothing" IN CONTEMPT.
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF greatest-from REGARDING entries AND 1.

THE OFFICE OF greatest-from, CONCERNING entries AND index.
    SHOULD index EQUAL THE LENGTH OF entries, REMAND WITH THE ITEM AT index IN entries.
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF maximum REGARDING (THE ITEM AT index IN entries) AND (THE FINDING OF greatest-from REGARDING entries AND index PLUS 1).

THE OFFICE OF reversal-of, CONCERNING entries.
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF reversal-from REGARDING entries AND THE LENGTH OF entries AND AN EMPTY SCHEDULE.

THE OFFICE OF reversal-from, CONCERNING entries AND index AND accumulated.
    SHOULD index FAIL TO EXCEED 0, REMAND WITH accumulated.
    ANNEX THE ITEM AT index IN entries TO accumulated.
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF reversal-from REGARDING entries AND index LESS 1 AND accumulated.

THE OFFICE OF tally-of, CONCERNING entries AND sought.
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF tally-from REGARDING entries AND sought AND 1.

THE OFFICE OF tally-from, CONCERNING entries AND sought AND index.
    SHOULD index EXCEED THE LENGTH OF entries, REMAND WITH 0.
    SHOULD (THE ITEM AT index IN entries) EQUAL sought, REMAND WITH 1 PLUS (THE FINDING OF tally-from REGARDING entries AND sought AND index PLUS 1).
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF tally-from REGARDING entries AND sought AND index PLUS 1.

THE OFFICE OF containment-of, CONCERNING entries AND sought.
    SHOULD THE FINDING OF tally-of REGARDING entries AND sought EXCEED 0, REMAND WITH SUSTAINED.
    REMAND WITH OVERRULED.
